 "script": {
  "hook": "Design media upload in chat that survives a dead network mid-video.",
  "question": "Design media upload for a chat app.",
  "trap": "The trap: attach the file to the request. Big videos time out, and restart from zero on every drop.",
  "steps": [
   "Upload first, send second. Store the bytes, then send a message that points to them.",
   "Chunk and resume. Split big files into chunks. After a drop, send only what is missing.",
   "Preview on device. Show a thumbnail at once, with progress. Let the user cancel.",
   "Pending state. Mark the message as sending until the upload finishes. Retry with backoff, even after a restart."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Upload the bytes first, send a pointer, and resume instead of restarting.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: group chat fan-out.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
